# Nov 16 2026 (KPC owner): LINE ENDINGS. The per-area 2-fer fingerprint (.github/scripts/kpc_fers_chain_plan.py area_fp)
# is worked out from the BYTES of the answer-key JSON files, and KPC-Links' answer-key rules hash works the same way over
# its rule files. Git for Windows writes CRLF on checkout by default, so a Windows checkout of the very same commit held
# different bytes than the club's own Linux builds. That is what stopped the PC 2-fer runner: its key gate called every
# green key stale and refused all 65 areas. These lines keep every checkout, on every machine, byte for byte what this
# repository holds: LF. area_fp also levels line endings itself, so this file is the second lock, not the only one.
*.json text eol=lf
*.geojson text eol=lf

# packed files are bytes already: git must never touch them
*.gz -text
*.zip -text
*.png -text
*.jpg -text
